-- A 3-operand ++ chain whose head has no static String type.  `acc` has no
-- type-forcing use before the `++`, so the emitter cannot pick the String path and
-- the chain stays on the runtime-dispatched fallback (mdk_append).  The result is
-- projected through stringLength.  Oracle: 7 (= length of "foobar!").

-- acc must stay unannotated: a String signature would type the head and move this
-- chain off the runtime-dispatched path it is meant to exercise.
-- lint-disable-next-line rule-missing-signature
-- The ++ chain is the thing under test, so interpolating it would test nothing.
-- lint-disable-next-line rule-concat-to-interp
build acc s = acc ++ s ++ "!"

main = stringLength (build "foo" "bar")
